# Docs & Rules Sync (required)

After **any** implementation that changes behavior, APIs, data, auth, config, or architecture — **before finishing the task** — update the affected docs and rules in the same change.

## What to update

| You changed                                      | Update                                              |
| ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |
| Routes, endpoints, auth on a route               | `server/docs/modules.md` + Swagger in `*.routes.js` |
| Mongoose schema, indexes, collections            | `server/docs/database-schema.md`                    |
| JWT, roles, permissions, password flow           | `server/docs/auth-flow.md`                          |
| Response shape, pagination, filters, rate limits | `server/docs/api-rules.md`                          |
| Modules, middleware, services, request flow      | `server/docs/architecture.md`                       |
| Env vars, ports, deploy steps, health check      | `server/docs/deployment.md` + `server/.env.example` |
| Project conventions or agent instructions        | `.cursor/rules/buytly-server.mdc`                   |

## Completion checklist

Do not mark the task done until:

1. Every row above that applies has been updated (or you explicitly confirm no doc impact).
2. Tests added/updated when behavior changed (`server/tests/`).
3. Implementation matches docs — docs describe **current** code, not planned behavior.

## When finishing

In your final response, include a short **Docs sync** line listing which doc files you updated (or "none — no API/schema/auth/config impact").
